/* book: lead: In a mixture of three or more species, every pair has its own diffusivity, and the flux of one species depends on the gradients of all the others. One effective D is no longer enough. The Stefan–Maxwell equations keep one friction term per pair; Wilke's formula collapses them into a single effective diffusivity for a species moving through a stagnant mixture of the others. This decides the size of */
